From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: clip a fullscreen window held in the normal state to its configured size

Lomiri (Ubuntu Touch) holds a game's fullscreen window in the normal state at 2400x1017 (the
screen less its top panel) until it grants fullscreen, and Wine reported the whole 2400x1080
Win32 window as the window geometry meanwhile. Once fullscreen was granted, Lomiri sent 2400x1017
and never the full 2400x1080 (stage 4.1, Ys: Memories of Celceta: the picture 63 px short, the
wallpaper below it, until a trip through the app switcher); qtmir skips a resize to the size it
believes the window already has, which this probably was. A window that wants fullscreen and is
held in the normal state at a known size is now clipped to that size, as a maximized one is.
---

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -566,11 +566,19 @@
                                                  int width, int height)
 {
     RECT rect;
+    /* UTDeck: a window that wants fullscreen but is held in the normal state at a given size
+     * (Lomiri, before it grants fullscreen or after it took it away) is clipped to that size too,
+     * like a maximized one. Reporting the whole fullscreen-sized window instead probably let Lomiri
+     * (qtmir) believe the window already had the full screen size, so it skipped the resize to it
+     * once fullscreen was granted: the picture stayed 63 px short under a hidden top panel. */
+    BOOL held_normal = (surface->window.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) &&
+                       !(surface->current.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) &&
+                       surface->current.width && surface->current.height;
 
     /* If the window size is bigger than the current state accepts, use the
      * largest visible (from Windows' perspective) subregion of the window. */
-    if ((surface->current.state & (WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED |
-                                   WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN)) &&
+    if (((surface->current.state & (WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED |
+                                    WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN)) || held_normal) &&
         (width > surface->current.width || height > surface->current.height))
     {
         wayland_surface_get_rect_in_monitor(surface, &rect);
